{"surah": 68, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "نٓۚ وَٱلْقَلَمِ وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ ", "translation": "Nūn.[1] By the pen and what they inscribe,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "نٓ", "translit": "ٓn", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَٱلْقَلَمِ", "translit": "ِmَlَqْlٱَw", "root": "قلم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَسْطُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُṭْsَy", "root": "سطر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "مَآ أَنتَ بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ بِمَجْنُونٍ ", "translation": "You are not, [O Muḥammad], by the favor of your Lord, a madman.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِنِعْمَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَmْʿعِnِb", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِمَجْنُونٍ", "translit": "ٍnwُnْjgَmِb", "root": "جنن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَإِنَّ لَكَ لَأَجْرًا غَيْرَ مَمْنُونٍ ", "translation": "And indeed, for you is a reward uninterrupted.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكَ", "translit": "َkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَأَجْرًا", "translit": "āًrْjgَaʾَl", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "غَيْرَ", "translit": "َrْyَغ", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَمْنُونٍ", "translit": "ٍnwُnْmَm", "root": "منن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَإِنَّكَ لَعَلَىٰ خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ ", "translation": "And indeed, you are of a great moral character.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَعَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خُلُقٍ", "translit": "ٍqُlُhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَظِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِẓَʿع", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "فَسَتُبْصِرُ وَيُبْصِرُونَ ", "translation": "So you will see and they will see", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَسَتُبْصِرُ", "translit": "ُrِṣْbُtَsَf", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَيُبْصِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِṣْbُyَw", "root": "بصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "بِأَييِّكُمُ ٱلْمَفْتُونُ ", "translation": "Which of you is the afflicted [by a devil].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بِأَييِّكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkِّyyَaʾِb", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمَفْتُونُ", "translit": "ُnwُtْfَmْlٱ", "root": "فتن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "إِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ أَعْلَمُ بِمَن ضَلَّ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦ وَهُوَ أَعْلَمُ بِٱلْمُهْتَدِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, your Lord is most knowing of who has gone astray from His way, and He is most knowing of the [rightly] guided.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِمَن", "translit": "nَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ضَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "سَبِيلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlyِbَs", "root": "سبل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِٱلْمُهْتَدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdَtْhُmْlٱِb", "root": "هدي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "فَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلْمُكَذِّبِينَ ", "translation": "Then do not obey the deniers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تُطِعِ", "translit": "ِʿعِṭُt", "root": "طوع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُكَذِّبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِّhdَkُmْlٱ", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "وَدُّوا۟ لَوْ تُدْهِنُ فَيُدْهِنُونَ ", "translation": "They wish that you would soften [in your position], so they would soften [toward you].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَدُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّdَw", "root": "ودد"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَوْ", "translit": "ْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تُدْهِنُ", "translit": "ُnِhْdُt", "root": "دهن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَيُدْهِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِhْdُyَf", "root": "دهن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَلَا تُطِعْ كُلَّ حَلَّافٍ مَّهِينٍ ", "translation": "And do not obey every worthless habitual swearer", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تُطِعْ", "translit": "ْʿعِṭُt", "root": "طوع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كُلَّ", "translit": "َّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حَلَّافٍ", "translit": "ٍfāَّlَḥ", "root": "حلف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَّهِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِhَّm", "root": "مهن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "هَمَّازٍ مَّشَّآءٍۭ بِنَمِيمٍ ", "translation": "[And] scorner, going about with malicious gossip -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "هَمَّازٍ", "translit": "ٍzāَّmَh", "root": "همز"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَّشَّآءٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭءٓāَّhsَّm", "root": "مشي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِنَمِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِmَnِb", "root": "نمم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "مَّنَّاعٍ لِّلْخَيْرِ مُعْتَدٍ أَثِيمٍ ", "translation": "A preventer of good, transgressing and sinful,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَّنَّاعٍ", "translit": "ٍʿعāَّnَّm", "root": "منع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِّلْخَيْرِ", "translit": "ِrْyَhkْlِّl", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُعْتَدٍ", "translit": "ٍdَtْʿعُm", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَثِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِhtَaʾ", "root": "اثم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "عُتُلٍّۭ بَعْدَ ذَٰلِكَ زَنِيمٍ ", "translation": "Cruel, moreover, and an illegitimate pretender.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عُتُلٍّۭ", "translit": "ٍّۭlُtُʿع", "root": "عتل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَعْدَ", "translit": "َdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "زَنِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِnَz", "root": "زنم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "أَن كَانَ ذَا مَالٍ وَبَنِينَ ", "translation": "Because he is a possessor of wealth and children,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَا", "translit": "āَhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَالٍ", "translit": "ٍlāَm", "root": "مول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَبَنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnَbَw", "root": "بني"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "إِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِ ءَايَٰتُنَا قَالَ أَسَٰطِيرُ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ ", "translation": "When Our verses are recited to him, he says, \"Legends of the former peoples.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تُتْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْtُt", "root": "تلو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتُنَا", "translit": "āَnُtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَسَٰطِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِṭَٰsَaʾ", "root": "سطر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "سَنَسِمُهُۥ عَلَى ٱلْخُرْطُومِ ", "translation": "We will brand him upon the snout.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَنَسِمُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُmِsَnَs", "root": "وسم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْخُرْطُومِ", "translit": "ِmwُṭْrُhkْlٱ", "root": "خرطم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "إِنَّا بَلَوْنَٰهُمْ كَمَا بَلَوْنَآ أَصْحَٰبَ ٱلْجَنَّةِ إِذْ أَقْسَمُوا۟ لَيَصْرِمُنَّهَا مُصْبِحِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, We have tried them as We tried the companions of the garden, when they swore to cut its fruit in the [early] morning", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَلَوْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْwَlَb", "root": "بلو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَمَا", "translit": "āَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَلَوْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْwَlَb", "root": "بلو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَصْحَٰبَ", "translit": "َbَٰḥْṣَaʾ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْجَنَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّnَjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَقْسَمُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmَsْqَaʾ", "root": "قسم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَيَصْرِمُنَّهَا", "translit": "āَhَّnُmِrْṣَyَl", "root": "صرم"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مُصْبِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِbْṣُm", "root": "صبح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "وَلَا يَسْتَثْنُونَ ", "translation": "Without making exception.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَسْتَثْنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnْhtَtْsَy", "root": "ثني"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "فَطَافَ عَلَيْهَا طَآئِفٌ مِّن رَّبِّكَ وَهُمْ نَآئِمُونَ ", "translation": "So there came upon it [i.e., the garden] an affliction from your Lord while they were asleep.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَطَافَ", "translit": "َfāَṭَf", "root": "طوف"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهَا", "translit": "āَhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "طَآئِفٌ", "translit": "ٌfِyʾٓāَṭ", "root": "طوف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَّبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نَآئِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِyʾٓāَn", "root": "نوم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "فَأَصْبَحَتْ كَٱلصَّرِيمِ ", "translation": "And it became as though reaped.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَصْبَحَتْ", "translit": "ْtَḥَbْṣَaʾَf", "root": "صبح"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَٱلصَّرِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِrَّṣlٱَk", "root": "صرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "فَتَنَادَوْا۟ مُصْبِحِينَ ", "translation": "And they called one another at morning,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَتَنَادَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَdāَnَtَf", "root": "ندي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مُصْبِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِbْṣُm", "root": "صبح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "أَنِ ٱغْدُوا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْثِكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ صَٰرِمِينَ ", "translation": "[Saying], \"Go early to your crop if you would cut the fruit.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَنِ", "translit": "ِnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱغْدُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُdْغٱ", "root": "غدو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حَرْثِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِhtْrَḥ", "root": "حرث"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "صَٰرِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِrَٰṣ", "root": "صرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "فَٱنطَلَقُوا۟ وَهُمْ يَتَخَٰفَتُونَ ", "translation": "So they set out, while lowering their voices,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱنطَلَقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَlَṭnٱَf", "root": "طلق"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَتَخَٰفَتُونَ", "translit": "َnwُtَfَٰhkَtَy", "root": "خفت"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "أَن لَّا يَدْخُلَنَّهَا ٱلْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكُم مِّسْكِينٌ ", "translation": "[Saying], \"There will surely not enter it today upon you [any] poor person.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَدْخُلَنَّهَا", "translit": "āَhَّnَlُhkْdَy", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyْlٱ", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُم", "translit": "mُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِّسْكِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِkْsِّm", "root": "سكن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "وَغَدَوْا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْدٍ قَٰدِرِينَ ", "translation": "And they went early in determination, [assuming themselves] able.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَغَدَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَdَغَw", "root": "غدو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَرْدٍ", "translit": "ٍdْrَḥ", "root": "حرد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَٰدِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِdَٰq", "root": "قدر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "فَلَمَّا رَأَوْهَا قَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّا لَضَآلُّونَ ", "translation": "But when they saw it, they said, \"Indeed, we are lost;", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَأَوْهَا", "translit": "āَhْwَaʾَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَضَآلُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّlٓāَḍَl", "root": "ضلل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "بَلْ نَحْنُ مَحْرُومُونَ ", "translation": "Rather, we have been deprived.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَحْرُومُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmwُrْḥَm", "root": "حرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "قَالَ أَوْسَطُهُمْ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكُمْ لَوْلَا تُسَبِّحُونَ ", "translation": "The most moderate of them said, \"Did I not say to you, 'Why do you not exalt [Allāh]?'\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَوْسَطُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُṭَsْwَaʾ", "root": "وسط"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَقُل", "translit": "lُqَaʾ", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَوْلَا", "translit": "āَlْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تُسَبِّحُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḥِّbَsُt", "root": "سبح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 29, "text": "قَالُوا۟ سُبْحَٰنَ رَبِّنَآ إِنَّا كُنَّا ظَٰلِمِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"Exalted is our Lord! Indeed, we were wrongdoers.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سُبْحَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰḥْbُs", "root": "سبح"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ظَٰلِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِlَٰẓ", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 30, "text": "فَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَلَٰوَمُونَ ", "translation": "Then they approached one another, blaming each other.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَقْبَلَ", "translit": "َlَbْqَaʾَf", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَعْضُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَعْضٍ", "translit": "ٍḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَتَلَٰوَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَwَٰlَtَy", "root": "لوم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 31, "text": "قَالُوا۟ يَٰوَيْلَنَآ إِنَّا كُنَّا طَٰغِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"O woe to us; indeed we were transgressors.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰوَيْلَنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَlْyَwَٰy", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "طَٰغِينَ", "translit": "َnyِغَٰṭ", "root": "طغي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 32, "text": "عَسَىٰ رَبُّنَآ أَن يُبْدِلَنَا خَيْرًا مِّنْهَآ إِنَّآ إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا رَٰغِبُونَ ", "translation": "Perhaps our Lord will substitute for us [one] better than it. Indeed, we are toward our Lord desirous.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عَسَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَsَʿع", "root": "عسي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبُّنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُبْدِلَنَا", "translit": "āَnَlِdْbُy", "root": "بدل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "خَيْرًا", "translit": "āًrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِّنْهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رَبِّنَا", "translit": "āَnِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَٰغِبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِغَٰr", "root": "رغب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 33, "text": "كَذَٰلِكَ ٱلْعَذَابُۖ وَلَعَذَابُ ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ أَكْبَرُۚ لَوْ كَانُوا۟ يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "Such is the punishment [of this world]. And the punishment of the Hereafter is greater, if they only knew.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابُ", "translit": "ُbāَhdَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَلَعَذَابُ", "translit": "ُbāَhdَʿعَlَw", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَكْبَرُ", "translit": "ُrَbْkَaʾ", "root": "كبر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَوْ", "translit": "ْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 34, "text": "إِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ", "translation": "Indeed, for the righteous with their Lord are the Gardens of Pleasure.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِلْمُتَّقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqَّtُmْlِl", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عِندَ", "translit": "َdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَبِّهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "جَنَّٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَّٰnَjg", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلنَّعِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِʿعَّnlٱ", "root": "نعم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 35, "text": "أَفَنَجْعَلُ ٱلْمُسْلِمِينَ كَٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ ", "translation": "Then will We treat the Muslims like the criminals?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَنَجْعَلُ", "translit": "ُlَʿعْjgَnَfَaʾ", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسْلِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِlْsُmْlٱ", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِrْjgُmْlٱَk", "root": "جرم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 36, "text": "مَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُونَ ", "translation": "What is [the matter] with you? How do you judge?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَحْكُمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmُkْḥَt", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 37, "text": "أَمْ لَكُمْ كِتَٰبٌ فِيهِ تَدْرُسُونَ ", "translation": "Or do you have a scripture in which you learn", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كِتَٰبٌ", "translit": "ٌbَٰtِk", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَدْرُسُونَ", "translit": "َnwُsُrْdَt", "root": "درس"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 38, "text": "إِنَّ لَكُمْ فِيهِ لَمَا تَخَيَّرُونَ ", "translation": "That indeed for you is whatever you choose?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَمَا", "translit": "āَmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَخَيَّرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَّyَhkَt", "root": "خير"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 39, "text": "أَمْ لَكُمْ أَيْمَٰنٌ عَلَيْنَا بَٰلِغَةٌ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِۙ إِنَّ لَكُمْ لَمَا تَحْكُمُونَ ", "translation": "Or do you have oaths [binding] upon Us, extending until the Day of Resurrection, that indeed for you is whatever you judge?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَيْمَٰنٌ", "translit": "ٌnَٰmْyَaʾ", "root": "يمن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَٰلِغَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَغِlَٰb", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَوْمِ", "translit": "ِmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَmَٰyِqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَمَا", "translit": "āَmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "تَحْكُمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmُkْḥَt", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 40, "text": "سَلْهُمْ أَيُّهُم بِذَٰلِكَ زَعِيمٌ ", "translation": "Ask them which of them, for that [claim], is responsible.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَلْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْlَs", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَيُّهُم", "translit": "mُhُّyَaʾ", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "زَعِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِʿعَz", "root": "زعم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 41, "text": "أَمْ لَهُمْ شُرَكَآءُ فَلْيَأْتُوا۟ بِشُرَكَآئِهِمْ إِن كَانُوا۟ صَٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "Or do they have partners?[1] Then let them bring their partners, if they should be truthful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "شُرَكَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَkَrُhs", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَلْيَأْتُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُtْaʾَyْlَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِشُرَكَآئِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِyʾٓāَkَrُhsِb", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "صَٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَٰṣ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 42, "text": "يَوْمَ يُكْشَفُ عَن سَاقٍ وَيُدْعَوْنَ إِلَى ٱلسُّجُودِ فَلَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ ", "translation": "The Day the shin will be uncovered[1] and they are invited to prostration but they [i.e., the disbelievers] will not be able,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُكْشَفُ", "translit": "ُfَhsْkُy", "root": "كشف"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَاقٍ", "translit": "ٍqāَs", "root": "سوق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَيُدْعَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَʿعْdُyَw", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلسُّجُودِ", "translit": "ِdwُjgُّslٱ", "root": "سجد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَسْتَطِيعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعyِṭَtْsَy", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 43, "text": "خَٰشِعَةً أَبْصَٰرُهُمْ تَرْهَقُهُمْ ذِلَّةٌۖ وَقَدْ كَانُوا۟ يُدْعَوْنَ إِلَى ٱلسُّجُودِ وَهُمْ سَٰلِمُونَ ", "translation": "Their eyes humbled, humiliation will cover them. And they used to be invited to prostration while they were sound.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "خَٰشِعَةً", "translit": "ًẗَʿعِhsَٰhk", "root": "خشع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَبْصَٰرُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُrَٰṣْbَaʾ", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَرْهَقُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُqَhْrَt", "root": "رهق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ذِلَّةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَّlِhd", "root": "ذلل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يُدْعَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَʿعْdُy", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلسُّجُودِ", "translit": "ِdwُjgُّslٱ", "root": "سجد"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "سَٰلِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِlَٰs", "root": "سلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 44, "text": "فَذَرْنِى وَمَن يُكَذِّبُ بِهَٰذَا ٱلْحَدِيثِۖ سَنَسْتَدْرِجُهُم مِّنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "So leave Me, [O Muḥammad], with [the matter of] whoever denies this statement [i.e., the Qur’ān]. We will progressively lead them [to punishment] from where they do not know.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَذَرْنِى", "translit": "àِnْrَhdَf", "root": "وذر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُكَذِّبُ", "translit": "ُbِّhdَkُy", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِهَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْحَدِيثِ", "translit": "ِhtyِdَḥْlٱ", "root": "حدث"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَنَسْتَدْرِجُهُم", "translit": "mُhُjgِrْdَtْsَnَs", "root": "درج"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "حَيْثُ", "translit": "ُhtْyَḥ", "root": "حيث"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 45, "text": "وَأُمْلِى لَهُمْۚ إِنَّ كَيْدِى مَتِينٌ ", "translation": "And I will give them time. Indeed, My plan is firm.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأُمْلِى", "translit": "àِlْmُaʾَw", "root": "ملو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَيْدِى", "translit": "àِdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَتِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِtَm", "root": "متن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 46, "text": "أَمْ تَسْـَٔلُهُمْ أَجْرًا فَهُم مِّن مَّغْرَمٍ مُّثْقَلُونَ ", "translation": "Or do you ask of them a payment, so they are by debt burdened down?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَسْـَٔلُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُlَٔـْsَt", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَجْرًا", "translit": "āًrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَهُم", "translit": "mُhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَّغْرَمٍ", "translit": "ٍmَrْغَّm", "root": "غرم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُّثْقَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَqْhtُّm", "root": "ثقل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 47, "text": "أَمْ عِندَهُمُ ٱلْغَيْبُ فَهُمْ يَكْتُبُونَ ", "translation": "Or have they [knowledge of] the unseen, so they write [it] down?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عِندَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْغَيْبُ", "translit": "ُbْyَغْlٱ", "root": "غيب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَكْتُبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbُtْkَy", "root": "كتب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 48, "text": "فَٱصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تَكُن كَصَاحِبِ ٱلْحُوتِ إِذْ نَادَىٰ وَهُوَ مَكْظُومٌ ", "translation": "Then be patient for the decision of your Lord, [O Muḥammad], and be not like the companion of the fish [i.e., Jonah] when he called out while he was distressed.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱصْبِرْ", "translit": "ْrِbْṣٱَf", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِحُكْمِ", "translit": "ِmْkُḥِl", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَكُن", "translit": "nُkَt", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَصَاحِبِ", "translit": "ِbِḥāَṣَk", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْحُوتِ", "translit": "ِtwُḥْlٱ", "root": "حوت"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "نَادَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَdāَn", "root": "ندي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مَكْظُومٌ", "translit": "ٌmwُẓْkَm", "root": "كظم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 49, "text": "لَّوْلَآ أَن تَدَٰرَكَهُۥ نِعْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ لَنُبِذَ بِٱلْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ مَذْمُومٌ ", "translation": "If not that a favor [i.e., mercy] from his Lord overtook him, he would have been thrown onto the naked shore while he was censured.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَّوْلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlْwَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَدَٰرَكَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَkَrَٰdَt", "root": "درك"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "نِعْمَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَmْʿعِn", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَّبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَنُبِذَ", "translit": "َhdِbُnَl", "root": "نبذ"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِٱلْعَرَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَrَʿعْlٱِb", "root": "عري"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَذْمُومٌ", "translit": "ٌmwُmْhdَm", "root": "ذمم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 50, "text": "فَٱجْتَبَٰهُ رَبُّهُۥ فَجَعَلَهُۥ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ", "translation": "And his Lord chose him and made him of the righteous.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱجْتَبَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰbَtْjgٱَf", "root": "جبي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبُّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَجَعَلَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَlَʿعَjgَf", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 51, "text": "وَإِن يَكَادُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَيُزْلِقُونَكَ بِأَبْصَٰرِهِمْ لَمَّا سَمِعُوا۟ ٱلذِّكْرَ وَيَقُولُونَ إِنَّهُۥ لَمَجْنُونٌ ", "translation": "And indeed, those who disbelieve would almost make you slip with their eyes [i.e., looks] when they hear the message, and they say, \"Indeed, he is mad.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَكَادُ", "translit": "ُdāَkَy", "root": "كود"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَيُزْلِقُونَكَ", "translit": "َkَnwُqِlْzُyَl", "root": "زلق"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِأَبْصَٰرِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِrَٰṣْbَaʾِb", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "سَمِعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعِmَs", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلذِّكْرَ", "translit": "َrْkِّhdlٱ", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَيَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَyَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَمَجْنُونٌ", "translit": "ٌnwُnْjgَmَl", "root": "جنن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 52, "text": "وَمَا هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "But it is not except a reminder to the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ذِكْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِّلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlِّl", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"4": [{"arabic": "فالسخاء خلق من أخلاق الله تعالى؛ والإيثار أعلى درجات السخاء. وكان ذلك من أدب رسول الله ﷺ حتى سماه الله تعالى عظيماً فقال تعالى \"وإنك لعلى خلق عظيم\" وقلا سهل بن عبد الله التستري قال موسى عليه السلام، يا رب أرني بعض درجات محمد ﷺ وأمته! فقال يا موسى إنك لن تطيق ذلك، ولكن أريك منزلة من منازله جليلة عظيمة فضلته بها عليك وعلى جميع خلقي، قال فكشف له عن ملكوت السموات فنظر إلى منزلة كادت تتلف نفسه من أنوارها وقربها من الله تعالى، فقال: يا رب بماذا بلغت به إلى هذه الكرامة؟ قال: بخلق اختصصته به من بينهم وه", "english": "Generosity (Sakhā') is a character trait from the character traits of Allah the Exalted; and preferring others over oneself (Īthār) is the highest degree of generosity. And that was from the refined character (Adab) of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until Allah the Exalted called him great, so He the Exalted said: \"And indeed, you are upon a great character (Khuluq 'Aẓīm).\" And Sahl ibn 'Abdillah al-Tustarī said: Mūsā, peace be upon him, said: O Lord, show me some of the degrees of Muḥammad ﷺ and his community! He said: O Mūsā, you will not be able to bear that, but I will show you a station from his stations, magnificent and great, with which I have favored him over you and over all My creation. He said: So He unveiled for him the dominion (Malakūt) of the heavens, and he looked at a station that almost destroyed his soul (Nafs) from its lights and its nearness to Allah the Exalted. He said: O Lord, by what did You bring him to this honor? He said: By a character trait with which I singled him out from among them, and it is preferring others over oneself (Īthār). O Mūsā, none of them comes to Me having acted upon it for a period of his life except that I feel ashamed (Istahyaytu) from calling him to account, and I settle him in My Garden (Jannah) wherever he wishes.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book-7a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Miserliness and Love of Wealth", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Condemnation of Miserliness and Love of Wealth'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "بيان فضيلة حسن الخلق ومذمة سوء الخلق\n\nقال الله تعالى لنبيه وحبيبه مثنياً عليه ومظهراً نعمته لديه \"وإنك لعلى خلق عظيم\" وقالت عائشة رضي الله عنها كان رسول الله ﭬ خلقه القرآن\"[1] وسأل رجل رسول الله ﭬ عن حسن الخلق فتلا قوله تعالى \"خذ العفو وأمر بالعرف واعرض عن الجاهلين\" ثم قال ﭬ \"هو أن تصل قطعك وتعطي من حرمك وتعفو ظلمك\"[2] وقال ﭬ: \"إنما بعثت لأتمم مكارم الأخلاق\"[3] وقال ﭬ \"أُقل ما يوضع في الميزان يوم القيامة تقوى الله وحسن الخلق\"[4] وجاء رجل إلى رسول الله ﭬ من بين يديه فقال: يا رسول الله ما الدين؟ ق", "english": "Explanation of the virtue of good character (Khuluq) and the censure of bad character (Khuluq).\n\nAllah the Exalted said to His Prophet and beloved, praising him and manifesting His favor upon him: \"And indeed, you are upon a great character (Khuluq)\" (Quran 68:4). And Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: \"The Messenger of Allah's character (Khuluq) was the Quran.\"[1] And a man asked the Messenger of Allah about good character (Khuluq), so he recited the saying of Allah the Exalted: \"Take what is given freely, enjoin what is recognized (Ma'ruf), and turn away from the ignorant.\" Then he said: \"It is that you join what is severed from you, give to one who deprives you, and pardon one who wrongs you.\"[2] And he said: \"I was only sent to perfect noble character (Akhlaq).\"[3] And he said: \"The least that is placed in the scale on the Day of Resurrection is the God-consciousness (Taqwa) of Allah and good character (Khuluq).\"[4] And a man came to the Messenger of Allah from before him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is religion (Deen)? He said: \"Good character (Khuluq).\" Then he came to him from his right side and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is religion (Deen)? He said: \"Good character (Khuluq).\" Then he came to him from his left side and said: What is religion (Deen)? He said: \"Good character (Khuluq).\" Then he came to him from behind him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is religion (Deen)? He turned to him and said: \"Do you not understand? It is that you do not become angry.\"[5] And it was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is misfortune? He said: \"Bad character (Khuluq).\"[6] And a man said to the Messenger of Allah: Advise me. He said: \"Fear Allah wherever you are.\" He said: Increase me. He said: \"Follow a bad deed with a good deed that erases it.\" He said: Increase me. He said: \"Treat people with good character (Khuluq).\"[7] And he was asked, peace be upon him: Which deeds are best? He said: \"Good character (Khuluq).\" And he said: \"Allah does not beautify the creation (Khalq) and character (Khuluq) of a servant and then feed him to the Fire.\"[8] And Al-Fudayl said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah, prayers and peace be upon him and his family: Indeed, then.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book2a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Breaking the Two Desires", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Breaking the Two Desires'", "badge": "Afterlife"}, {"arabic": "وأولى ما يمتحن به حسن الخلق الصبر على الأذى واحتمال الجفاء، ومن شكا من سوء خلق غيره دل ذلك على سوء خلقه، فإن حسن الخلق احتمال الأذى فقد روي أن رسول الله ﭬ كان يوماً يمشي ومعه أنس فأدركه أعرابي فجذبه جذباً شديداً وكان عليه برد نجراني غليظ الحاشية، قال أنس رضي الله عنه: حتى نظرت إلى عنق رسول الله ﭬ قد أثرت فيه حاشية البرد من شدة جذبه، فقال: يا محمد هب لي من مال الله الذي عندك، فالتفت إليه رسول الله ﭬ وضحك، ثم أمر بإعطائه[58] ولما أكثرت قريش إيذاءه وضربه قال: اللهم اغفر لقومي فإنهم لا يعلمون\"[59] ق", "english": "And the foremost thing by which good character (Khuluq) is tested is patience (Sabr) upon harm and enduring harshness, and whoever complains of the bad character of another indicates thereby his own bad character, for good character is enduring harm. It has been narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking one day with Anas when a Bedouin caught up to him and pulled him with a strong pull, and he was wearing a thick-edged Najrani cloak. Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Until I looked at the neck of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saw the mark of the cloak's edge upon it from the severity of his pulling.' He said: 'O Muhammad, grant me from the wealth of Allah that is with you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to him and smiled, then ordered that he be given. And when the Quraysh increased in harming him and striking him, he said: 'O Allah, forgive my people for they do not know.' It is said that this was on the day of Uhud, therefore Allah the Exalted revealed: 'And indeed, you are upon a great character (Khuluq).'", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book2a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Breaking the Two Desires", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication, from 'Breaking the Two Desires'", "badge": "Hadith"}, {"arabic": "ثم لما أكمل الله تعالى خلقه أثنى عليه فقال تعالى وإنك لعلى خلق عظيم فسبحانه ما أعظم شأنه وأتم امتنانه ثم انظر إلى عميم لطفه وعظيم فضله كيف أعطى ثم أثنى فهو الذي زينه بالخلق الكريم ثم أضاف إليه ذلك فقال وإنك لعلى خلق عظيم", "english": "Then when Allah the Exalted perfected his creation, He praised him, saying: 'And indeed, you are upon a great character (Khuluq 'Adheem).' So glory be to Him, how great is His affair and how complete is His favor. Then look at the vastness of His gentleness and the greatness of His grace—how He gave and then praised. For He is the One who adorned him with the noble character (Khuluq Kareem), then attributed that to him, saying: 'And indeed, you are upon a great character (Khuluq 'Adheem).'", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Living and Prophetic Character", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Etiquette of Living and Prophetic Character'", "badge": "General"}, {"arabic": "فضيلة الألفة والأخوة أعلم أن الألفة ثمرة حسن الخلق والتفرق ثمرة سوء الخلق فحسن الخلق يوجب التحاب والتآلف والتوافق وسوء الخلق يثمر التباغض والتحاسد والتدابر ومهما كان المثمر محمودا كانت الثمرة محمودة وحسن الخلق لا تخفى في الدين فضيلته وهو الذي مدح الله سبحانه به نبيه عليه السلام إذ قال وإنك لعلى خلق عظيم وقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أكثر ما يدخل الناس الجنة تقوى الله وحسن الخلق حديث أول ما يدخل الجنة تقوى الله وحسن الخلق أخرجه الترمذي والحاكم من حديث أبي هريرة وقال صحيح الإسناد وقد تقدم", "english": "The virtue of affection and brotherhood: Know that affection is the fruit of good character (Khuluq) and separation is the fruit of bad character (Khuluq). Good character necessitates mutual love, affection, and harmony, while bad character produces mutual hatred, envy, and turning away. Whenever the producer is praiseworthy, the fruit is praiseworthy. The virtue of good character in the religion is not hidden, and it is that with which Allah, glorified be He, praised His Prophet, peace be upon him, when He said: 'And indeed, you are upon a great character (Khuluq).' And the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'The most that causes people to enter Paradise is the God-consciousness (Taqwa) of Allah and good character (Khuluq).' The hadith: 'The first to enter Paradise is the God-consciousness (Taqwa) of Allah and good character (Khuluq).' Al-Tirmidhi and Al-Hakim transmitted it from the narration of Abu Hurairah and said its chain is authentic, and it has preceded.", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k05.doc.txt", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "13": [{"arabic": "قال الله تعالى \"هماز مشاء بنميم\" ثم قال \"عتل بعد ذلك زنيم\" قال عبد الله بن المبارك: الزنيم ولد الزنا الذي لا يكتم الحديث، وأشار به إلى أن كل من لم يكتم الحديث ومشى بالنميمة دل على أنه ولد زنا استنباطاً من قوله عز وجل \"عتل بعد ذلك زنيم\" والزنيم هو الدعى", "english": "Allah the Exalted said: \"A slanderer, going about with calumny\" then said: \"Cruel, after that, base-born.\" Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak said: The base-born (Zanim) is the child of fornication who does not conceal speech, and he indicated by this that everyone who does not conceal speech and goes about with talebearing shows that he is a child of fornication, derived from His saying the Exalted: \"Cruel, after that, base-born.\" And the base-born (Zanim) is the one attributed falsely.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book4a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Anger and Hatred", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication, from 'Condemnation of Anger and Hatred'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "32": [{"arabic": "وتقول عند الخسران ﴿ عسى ربنا أن يبدلنا خيرا منها إنا إلى ربنا راغبون ﴾", "english": "And say at the time of loss: 'Perhaps our Lord will exchange for us better than it. Indeed, we are to our Lord desirous.'", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance", "badge": "Du'a"}], "35": [{"arabic": "فلو خرجت من مكمن الغرور وأنصفت نفسك يا رجل وكلنا ذلك الرجل لعلمت أنك من حين تصبح إلى حين تمسي لا تسعى إلا في الحظوظ العاجلة ولا تتحرك ولا تسكن إلا لعاجل الدنيا ثم تطمع أن تكون غدا من أمته وأتباعه وما أبعد ظنك وما أبرد طمعك ﴿ أفنجعل المسلمين كالمجرمين ما لكم كيف تحكمون ﴾ {} ولنرجع إلى ما كنا فيه وبصدده فقد امتد عنان الكلام إلى غير مقصده ولنذكر الآن من المنامات الكاشفة لأحوال الموتي ما يعظم الانتفاع به إذ ذهبت النبوة وبقيت المبشرات وليس ذلك إلا المنامات.", "english": "If you were to emerge from the abode of delusion and be just to your soul (Nafs), O man—and all of us are that man—you would know that from morning until evening you strive only for immediate gains, and you neither move nor rest except for the immediate worldly life. Then you hope to be tomorrow from his community (Ummah) and followers, and how distant is your assumption and how cold is your hope! 'Shall We then treat the Muslims like the criminals? What is [wrong] with you? How do you judge?' (Quran 68:35-36). And let us return to what we were in and concerning, for the reins of speech have extended beyond its intended purpose. And let us now mention from the dreams that reveal the states of the dead what greatly benefits from it, since prophethood has gone and the glad tidings remain, and that is nothing but the dreams.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "44": [{"arabic": "وهذا الغرور علاجه معرفة دلائل الكرامة والهوان إما بالبصيرة أو بالتقليد أما البصيرة فبأن يعرف وجه كون الالتفات إلى شهوات الدنيا مبعد عن الله ووجه كون التباعد عنها مقرباً إلى الله ويدرك ذلك بالإلهام في منازل العارفين والأولياء، وشرحه من جملة علوم المكاشفة ولا يليق بعلم المعاملة \"وأما معرفته بطريق التقليد والتصديق\" فهو أن يؤمن بكتاب الله تعالى ويصدق رسوله وقد قال تعالى \"أيحسبون أن ما نمدهم به من مال وبنين نسارع لهم في الخيرات بل لا يشعرون\" وقال تعالى \"سنستدرجهم من حيث لا يعلمون\" وقال تعالى \"فتحنا ع", "english": "And the cure for this delusion (Ghurur) is knowing the signs of honor (Karama) and humiliation (Hawan) either through insight (Bassira) or through imitation (Taqleed). As for insight, it is by knowing how turning toward the desires of the world distances from Allah and how distancing from them brings near to Allah, and one perceives that through inspiration (Ilham) in the stations of the knowers (Arifeen) and the friends (Awliya), and its explanation is among the sciences of unveiling (Mukashafa) and is not suitable for the science of transaction. \"And as for knowing it through the way of imitation and belief,\" it is to have faith in the Book of Allah the Exalted and believe His Messenger. And He the Exalted has said: \"Do they think that what We extend to them of wealth and children, We hasten for them in good things? Rather, they do not perceive.\" And He the Exalted has said: \"So leave Me with [the matter of] whoever denies this statement. We will progressively lead them [to destruction] from where they do not know.\" And He the Exalted has said: \"We opened to them the gates of every thing until, when they rejoiced in that which they were given, We seized them suddenly, and at once they were in despair.\" And in the interpretation of His saying the Exalted \"We will progressively lead them [to destruction] from where they do not know,\" it is that whenever they commit a sin, We grant them a blessing to increase their delusion. And He the Exalted has said: \"We only give them respite that they may increase in sin.\" And He the Exalted has said: \"And never think that Allah is unaware of what the wrongdoers do. He only delays them for a Day when eyes will stare [in horror].\" And other than that which has come in the Book of Allah the Exalted and the Sunnah of His Messenger. So whoever believes in it is freed from this delusion, for the origin of this delusion is ignorance of Allah and His attributes, for whoever knows Him does not feel secure from His plan (Makr) nor is deceived by such false imaginings, and looks at Pharaoh, Haman, and Korah and at the kings of the earth and what happened to them—how Allah was good to them initially then destroyed them utterly! So He the Exalted said: \"Do you perceive of them anyone?\" the verse. And Allah the Exalted has warned of His plan and gradual leading, saying: \"So none feels secure from the plan of Allah except the losing people.\" And He the Exalted has said: \"And they planned a plan, and We planned a plan, while they perceived not.\" And He the Mighty and Majestic has said: \"And they planned, and Allah planned. And Allah is the best of planners.\" And He the Exalted has said: \"Indeed, they are planning a plan, and I am planning a plan. So allow time for the disbelievers. Deal with them gently [for a while].\" So just as it is not permissible for the neglected servant to infer from the master's neglect of him and enabling.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book-10a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Delusion", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Condemnation of Delusion'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "الحمد لله الذي لا يتكل على عفوه ورحمته إلا الراجون، ولا يحذر سوء غضبه وسطوته إلا الخائفون، الذي استدرج عباده من حيث لا يعلمون، وسلط عليهم الشهوات وأمرهم بترك ما يشتهون، وابتلاهم بالغضب وكلفهم كظم الغيظ فيما يغضبون، ثم حفهم بالمكاره واللذات وأملى لهم لينظر كيف يعملون، وامتحن بهم حبهم ليعلم صدقهم فيما يدعون، وعرفهم أنه لا يخفى عليه شيء مما يسرون وما يعلنون، وحذرهم أن يأخذهم بغتة وهم لا يشعرون فقال \"ما ينظرون إلا صيحة واحدة تأخذهم وهم يخصمون فلا يستطيعون توصية ولا إلى أهلهم يرجعون\" والصلاة والسلام ", "english": "Praise be to Allah who none rely upon His pardon and His mercy except the hopeful ones, and none fear the evil of His anger and His might except the fearful ones, who gradually leads His servants from where they do not know, and empowered over them the desires and commanded them to abandon what they desire, and tested them with anger and obligated them to suppress rage in what angers them, then surrounded them with hardships and pleasures and gave them respite to see how they act, and tested through them their love to know their truthfulness in what they claim, and made known to them that nothing is hidden from Him of what they conceal and what they reveal, and warned them that He may seize them suddenly while they are unaware, so He said: \"They await not but a single blast which will seize them while they are disputing. Then they will not be able to make a bequest, nor will they return to their families.\" And prayers and peace be upon Muhammad His messenger under whose banner the prophets march, and upon his family and his companions the guided leaders, and the pleased masters, prayers equal in number to what has been of Allah's creation and what will be, and may the first and the last attain its blessing, and grant abundant peace.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book5a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Envy", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Condemnation of Envy'", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "ولذلك قال الله عز وجل: (ولا تطع من أغفلنا قلبه عن ذكرنا واتبع هواه وكان أمره فرط", "english": "And therefore Allah the Exalted said: (And do not obey one whose heart We have made heedless of Our Remembrance (Dhikr) and who follows his desire (Hawa) and whose affair is ever [in] neglect", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-1.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Insight"}], "48": [{"arabic": "ولم يحتمل ليونس عليه السلام ما دون هذا لما أقيم مقام القبض والهيبة، فعوقب بالسجن في بطن الحوت - في ظلمات ثلاث - ونودي عليه إلى يوم القيامة \" لولا أن تداركه نعمة من ربه لنبذ بالعراء وهو مذموم \". قال الحسن: العراء هو القيامة. ونهى نبينا ﭬ أن يقتدى به وقيل له: \" فاصبر لحكم ربك ولا تكن كصاحب الحوت إذ نادى وهو مكظوم \".", "english": "And it was not endured for Yunus (Jonah), peace be upon him, what was less than this because he was placed in the position of contraction (Qabd) and awe (Hibah), so he was punished with imprisonment in the belly of the whale - in three darknesses - and he was called upon until the Day of Resurrection: \"Had it not been that a favor from his Lord reached him, he would have been cast on the barren shore while he was blameworthy.\" Al-Hasan said: The barren shore (Al-'Ara') is the Resurrection. And our Prophet, peace be upon him, was prohibited from being followed in this, and it was said to him: \"So be patient for the decree of your Lord and do not be like the companion of the whale when he called out while he was suppressed.\"", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book6.doc.txt", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "49": [{"arabic": "ولكن في الحال مختلفان، فقال: \" وأما من جاءك يسعى  وهو  يخشى  فأنت  عنده تلهى \"، وقال في الآخر: \" أما من استغنى فأنت له تصدى \"  وةكذلك  أمره  بالقعود مع طائفة، فقال عز وجل: \" وإذا جاءك الذين يؤمنون بآياتنا  فقل  سلام  عليكم  \" وأمره بالإعراض عن غيرهم، فقال: \" وإذا رأيت  الذين  يخوضون  في  آياتنا  فأعرض عنهم \" حتى قال: \" فلا تقعد بعد الذكرى مع القوم  الظالمين  \"  وقال  تعالى:  \" واصبر نفسك مع الذين يدعون ربهم بالغداة والعشي \". فكذلك الانبساط والإدلال يحتمل من بعض العباد دون بعض. فمن  انبساط  الأنس", "english": "But in the state (Hāl) they differ, so He said: \"And as for he who comes to you striving while he fears, you are to him diverted,\" and in the other: \"As for he who considers himself self-sufficient, to him you give attention.\" And likewise He commanded him to sit with a group, so the Mighty and Majestic said: \"And when those who believe in Our signs come to you, say: Peace be upon you.\" And He commanded him to turn away from others, saying: \"And when you see those who engage in vain discourse concerning Our signs, then turn away from them\" until He said: \"Then do not sit after the Remembrance (Dhikr) with the wrongdoing people.\" And He said: \"And restrain yourself with those who call upon their Lord in the morning and the evening.\" Similarly, expansion (Inbisāt) and familiarity (Idlāl) are permissible for some worshippers and not others. From the expansion of intimacy (Uns) is the saying of Moses, peace be upon him: \"It is not except Your trial; You misguide with it whom You will and guide whom You will,\" and his saying in explanation and excuse when it was said to him: \"Go to Pharaoh,\" so he said: \"And they have upon me a sin,\" and his saying: \"Indeed, I fear that they will deny me and that my breast will tighten and my tongue will not be fluent,\" and his saying: \"Indeed, we fear that he will hasten against us or that he will transgress.\" And this from other than Moses, peace be upon him, would be from bad manners (Sū' al-Adab) because the one who is placed in the station (Maqām) of intimacy (Uns) is indulged and tolerated. And it was not tolerated for Jonah, peace be upon him, what is less than this because he was placed in the station of contraction (Qabd) and awe (Hībah), so he was punished with imprisonment in the belly of the whale - in three darknesses - and he was called out to until the Day of Resurrection: \"Had it not been that a favor (Ni'mah) from his Lord reached him, he would have been cast onto the open land (Al-'Arā') while he was blameworthy.\" Al-Hasan said: Al-'Arā' is the Resurrection. And our Prophet, peace be upon him, was prohibited from being followed in this, and it was said to him: \"So be patient for the decree of your Lord and do not be like the companion of the whale when he called out while he was distressed.\"", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book6.doc.txt", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 400, 1444], [2, 1444, 3854], [3, 3854, 5501], [4, 5501, 8474]], "2": [[1, 350, 1794], [2, 1794, 2690], [3, 2690, 4090], [4, 4090, 5140], [5, 5140, 7029]], "3": [[1, 350, 1633], [2, 1633, 2131], [3, 2131, 3638], [4, 3638, 4535], [5, 4535, 5905]], "4": [[1, 350, 1966], [2, 1966, 3437], [3, 3437, 4304], [4, 4304, 5618]], "5": [[1, 350, 2006], [2, 2006, 4260]], "6": [[1, 350, 2502], [2, 2502, 4260]], "7": [[1, 400, 1467], [2, 1467, 2563], [3, 2563, 3265], [4, 3265, 4551], [5, 4551, 5428], [6, 5428, 6320], [7, 6320, 6963], [8, 6963, 8571], [9, 8571, 9711], [10, 9711, 10997], [11, 10997, 13542]], "8": [[1, 350, 1293], [2, 1293, 2210], [3, 2210, 4495]], "9": [[1, 350, 1767], [2, 1767, 2325], [3